## Firmware (600) - MCU core safety

Glob-triggered safety for all MCU firmware, not STM32-only. Recipes: `.cursor/skills/sc-firmware/references/core.md`. This glob does not require CubeMX as a Must.

### Must

- Layer: `app/` includes only `hal_if/`; wrap vendor HAL behind `hal_if/`; `drivers/` / `bsp/` own vendor headers
- Fixed-width types (`stdint.h`); no recursion; no heap after init in hot paths or ISR; bounded loops
- Checked returns on non-void functions; restrict preprocessor to include guards and simple macros
- Keep ISR short: set flag / wake task only; shared vars `volatile` plus atomic or critical section
- FDIR: enable WDT and kick in the main loop; HardFault logs PC/LR to retained RAM when possible
- static analysis for flight-grade claims

### Must not

- Recursion; heap after init in hot paths or ISR; unbounded loops
- Ignore returns of non-void functions; heavy preprocessor (function-like control flow)
- `printf`, delay, blocking, or semaphore-take inside ISR
- Include vendor HAL headers from `app/`; skip `hal_if/` (`app/` -> `drivers/` directly)
- Circular includes across layers

STM32-target note: wrap generated `MX_*` in `bsp/` / `hal_if/` when that vendor path is in scope. CubeMX recipes belong to STM32 target refs, not this glob.
